  "r1": {
   "critique": [
    {
     "design": "r0A",
     "good": "The only design that produces any single-line rows (3 of 8), so it is the shortest table (400px) and the closest to a scannable card. Cols 1–2 are at their true minimum (61 = 40px text, 88 = 67px text), so nothing is wasted on the 'what + how much' pair, and the header 用量（克） sits unbroken right beside the numbers it qualifies. No mid-word splits.",
     "problems": "The 备注 column is visibly squeezed: notes break into two stubby lines even when they are short (生抽有咸味，谨防过咸, 去腥用，不喜酒味可减), and the breaks land after the comma, leaving a lonely second line that makes the row look like it is still loading. Row rhythm is choppy (33/53/33/53/53/33/33/53/53) with no pattern, because row height is set by whichever prose cell happens to wrap. Col 4 carries almost the whole 80px deficit while col 3 is also still wrapping its longest instruction.",
     "cause": "widths [61,88,179,151]: col4 gets only 130px of text against the 160px it needs, so every note above ~10 characters wraps; col3 gets 158px against 208px, so 切3厘米见方块，冷水下锅焯净血沫 also wraps. The deficit was split 29/9 in favour of col3, but 29px is not enough to save col3's long cell and 9px is not enough to save col4's short cells — the split falls between two useful thresholds."
    },
    {
     "design": "r0B",
     "good": "Col 3 is nearly satisfied (195px text vs 208 needed), so the operative instruction — the thing a cook actually acts on — reads almost in one line, and the 五花肉 row is only marginally wrapped. Cols 1–2 again at minimum, so no waste there.",
     "problems": "备注 is a disaster: 114px total = 93px text, so all 8 rows wrap, and the breaks are ugly and semantically wrong (去腥用，不喜酒 / 味可减, 生抽有咸味，谨 / 防过咸). A secondary advisory column now dictates the height of every single row: table is 440px, 40px taller than r0A, with 8/8 rows at 53px. The table no longer reads as rows — it reads as two tall text columns fighting each other.",
     "cause": "widths [61,88,216,114]: col4 was cut to 71% of its one-line need to buy col3 the last 21px it needed, but those 21px only un-wrap one cell (the longest instruction still does not fit), while the 67px taken from col4 un-wraps nothing and wraps everything. Worst possible trade: the sacrifice bought no row."
    },
    {
     "design": "r0C",
     "good": "Most relaxed-looking of the three: ingredient and amount columns have visible breathing room, headers sit comfortably, and the table feels calm and symmetric at first glance. Col 3 at 151px text keeps every instruction except the longest on one line.",
     "problems": "The calm is bought by stealing from the columns that need it. 食材 gets 59px of text for a 40px need (+19 dead px) and 用量 gets 77 for 67 (+10 dead px) — about 29px of pure slack that the prose columns are starving for. Result: 备注 at 108px text wraps 5 rows, table is 420px, i.e. 20px taller than r0A while *looking* emptier. The ragged 33/53 alternation is still there, and the dead space in cols 1–2 reads as a layout mistake rather than generosity because the neighbouring column is visibly cramped.",
     "cause": "widths [80,98,172,129]: +19px and +10px added to columns whose content cannot use them, taken directly out of col3 (−7px) and col4 (−22px). Since the one-line requirements are 40/67/208/160, every pixel above 40 and 67 is wasted, and every pixel below 208/160 costs a row."
    }
   ],
   "done": false,
   "names": [
    "r1A",
    "r1B",
    "r1C"
   ]
  }
 },
