   "idea": "New idea: give the two prose columns near-equal width (145/143px text) on the theory that they play the same role — free text read one row at a time — and that a calm, almost symmetric prose block reads better than a hierarchy the content does not really support (备注 notes are often as long as 处理方式 instructions). Keeps cols 1–2 minimal. Expect 3 double rows (五花肉, 冰糖, 料酒), but the wraps distribute evenly across both prose columns instead of dumping every break on 备注, so no column looks broken; table ≈357px.",
