 "understanding": {
  "purpose": "A kitchen reference card: eight ingredients for 家常红烧肉, each with a quantity and a short prep instruction plus an advisory note. It is consulted mid-cooking, not read as prose, so lookup speed and unambiguous quantities matter more than compactness.",
  "reading": "Vertical scan down col 1 to locate an ingredient, then a short rightward hop to its amount, then the prep instruction, then optionally the note. Comparison happens down the amount column (500 vs 15 vs 5) and across the two prose columns, which are read only one row at a time. Rows are the unit, so every row should keep its four cells visually on the same band and prose should wrap rather than push a row apart.",
  "groups": [
   "col 1 + col 2: ingredient and its quantity are one measure unit ('what' + 'how much') and must be read together, so they should stay narrow and adjacent with no wrapping between them",
   "col 3 + col 4: both are free prose; 处理方式 is the operative instruction, 备注 is secondary/advisory, so they may be traded against each other but not against cols 1–2"
  ],
  "keep_intact": [
   "ingredient names in col 1 (五花肉, 大葱, 冰糖 …) — never break a 2–3 character name",
   "all amounts in col 2: 500, 15, 20, 25, 30, 5 and the words 适量 / 少许 must sit on one line",
   "the header 用量（克） should stay unbroken so the unit is not orphaned from the number it qualifies",
   "numeral+unit tokens inside prose such as 3厘米 and 两次 should not be split mid-token"
  ],
  "may_wrap": [
   "处理方式 sentences (切3厘米见方块，冷水下锅焯净血沫 / 焯水和炖煮时分两次加入) — 2 lines is acceptable",
   "备注 sentences (选肥瘦三层分明的五花肉 / 老姜去腥效果更好) — advisory, can absorb 2–3 lines without hurting the lookup",
   "the header 处理方式 / 备注 may wrap only as a last resort; both fit at 27px unbreakable"
  ]
 }
